{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 update — refactored to Option B (reuse the existing per-candidate wrapper seam)\n\nThe first `review-plan` run returned **BLOCK** on plan hygiene (finding f4ae: the description didn't state HOW the leg marker reaches the exception `should_fall_back` inspects) plus advisories — one of which (f626) correctly observed that the separate `_FallbackLegModel` wrapper DUPLICATED the existing `wrap_candidate`/`_TracedCandidateModel` layer (which already stamps `_candidate_order`). Operator chose **Option B**: fold the marker into that existing wrapper.\n\n**What changed vs. the prior implementation:**\n- `tracing.py`: `_TracedCandidateModel.request()`'s existing `except` block now stamps `_FALLBACK_LEG_ATTR` when `_candidate_order > 0`; added the `_FALLBACK_LEG_ATTR` constant + `is_fallback_leg_failure(exc)` reader.\n- `model_classes.py`: `should_fall_back` reads `is_fallback_leg_failure(exc)` (from `rebar.llm.tracing`); the separate `_FallbackLegModel` + `_fallback_leg_wrapper_class` + `_tag_fallback_leg` + `_wrap_fallback_leg` + the `build_fallback_model` double-wrap are **removed** (net −59 LOC; file 680→621).\n- `failure.py` (Change 2): unchanged from validated state.\n\n**Fresh proofs after the refactor (all local, ZERO Bedrock load):**\n- RED-for-the-right-reason: stashing the 3 source files → the e2e reproduces bare `TypeError`/`NEEDS_INVESTIGATION`, the group tests misclassify as `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`. GREEN after: `test_throttle_no_failover_1c0d.py` 4 passed.\n- Mutation-with-teeth inside `sandbox-exec -f` (deny file-write* outside $PWD+scratch; no `timeout` binary on host): (a) revert Change 2 → group tests RED (killed); (b) revert the marker stamping → e2e RED reproducing the **exact** incident signature `{exception_type: TypeError, message: \"Could not resolve authentication method\", resolution_class: NEEDS_INVESTIGATION, retryable: False}` (killed). Both restored byte-identical (sha256 verified) → GREEN.\n- `make lint` PASS; complexity ratchet `new=0 increased=0`; module-size clean (failure 720 / model_classes 621 / tracing 311, all < 800); `make typecheck` clean (692 files); broad sweep `-k \"llm or fallback or failure or classif or candidate or runner or provider or model_class or tracing\"` = **1642 passed, 3 skipped**.\n\n**Surface-parity (unchanged by B):** both changes still land at the shared cores — Change 2 at `classify_llm_failure` via the single `run_failure.interpret_failure` (+ preflight) seam; Change 1 at the single `build_fallback_model` construction site (runner.py:467), and now specifically inside the wrapper EVERY candidate already gets. One fix, all gate surfaces (review-plan / verify-completion / review-code / claim / close).\n\n**Attribution unchanged:** caused_by `8fbd-e9d5-326e-40d8`, class `plan_defect` (both latent defects predate 8fbd, which activated them). Re-running the authorized single `review-plan` gate op next."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788055579354649900,"uuid":"3d596119-5acd-4a4a-9557-174902c8db0f"}